---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BrandMark from '../components/BrandMark.astro';
import PeerConnection from '../components/PeerConnection.astro';
import CallExample from '../components/CallExample.astro';
const docs = 'https://sdk.getaster.now';
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
const languages = [
  { name: 'Rust', logo: 'rust.svg' },
  { name: 'Python', logo: 'python.svg' },
  { name: 'TypeScript', logo: 'typescript.png' },
  { name: 'Go', logo: 'go.svg' },
  { name: 'Java', logo: 'java.png' },
  { name: 'Kotlin', logo: 'kotlin.svg' },
  { name: '.NET', logo: 'dotnet.svg' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Aster — Connect services across machines" description="Enterprise peer-to-peer application SDK. Typed RPC, cryptographic peer identity, and scoped access over Iroh.">
  <header class="site-header shell">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Aster home"><BrandMark />Aster</a>
    <nav aria-label="Primary"><a href="#examples">Examples</a><a href={`${docs}/docs/overview/what-is-aster`}>How it works</a><a href="/blog">Blog</a><a href={`${docs}/docs/`}>Docs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/aster-rpc/aster-rpc">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
  </header>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="intro shell" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
      <div class="intro-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Enterprise peer-to-peer application SDK</p>
        <h1 id="intro-title">Connect services<br/>across machines.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Your service might run in a cloud instance, a customer network, or on the machine under your desk. Aster gives you a way to call it by its cryptographic identity.</p>
        <p class="intro-detail">Define a typed service, connect to a peer, and control which calls it may make. One shared Rust engine, with APIs for different languages.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="start-link" href={`${docs}/docs/quickstart/python`}>Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${docs}/docs/concepts/transport`}>Understand the connection</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-diagram"><PeerConnection /></div>
    </section>

    <div class="foundation shell"><p>Built on</p><a href="https://iroh.computer">Iroh <span>connectivity</span></a><a href="https://fory.apache.org">Apache Fory <span>serialization</span></a><a href="https://github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3">BLAKE3 <span>contract identity</span></a><button type="button" data-motion-toggle aria-pressed="false" hidden>Pause motion</button></div>

    <section class="call-section shell" aria-labelledby="call-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A service and a call</p><h2 id="call-title">The interface lives in your code.</h2></div><p>Aster carries the call between peers. Your application defines the types, implements the handler, and decides who can use it.</p></div>
      <CallExample />
    </section>

    <section class="identity-section" aria-labelledby="identity-title">
      <div class="shell identity-layout">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Identity and access</p><h2 id="identity-title">Know which peer<br/>you’re talking to.</h2><p class="section-copy">A network address tells you where to send traffic. Aster’s peer identity tells you which endpoint is on the other side of the connection.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${docs}/docs/concepts/trust-model`}>Read the trust model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
        <dl class="identity-details">
          <div><dt><span>01</span> Keep an identity across network changes</dt><dd>Persist the endpoint key to keep the same identity when its IP address changes. Protect and back up that key.</dd></div>
          <div><dt><span>02</span> Authenticate the connection</dt><dd>Iroh establishes an encrypted connection and authenticates the remote peer. Direct and relay paths use the same peer identity.</dd></div>
          <div><dt><span>03</span> Authorize the work</dt><dd>Configure admission and method permissions for your application. Knowing a peer’s identity is the starting point for deciding what it may do.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="examples-section shell" id="examples" aria-labelledby="examples-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Put it to work</p><h2 id="examples-title">Start with something you can run.</h2></div><p>Follow one service from its first call through streaming and access control, or connect an existing service to an AI tool.</p></div>
      <a class="example-row" href={`${docs}/docs/quickstart/mission-control`}><span class="example-number">01</span><div><h3>MissionControl</h3><p>Build a DevOps control plane. Collect agent logs and metrics, issue remote commands, and scope operator access.</p></div><span class="example-link">Follow the walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
      <a class="example-row" href={`${docs}/docs/guides/mcp-integration`}><span class="example-number">02</span><div><h3>Remote tools with MCP</h3><p>Make an Aster service available to an AI application through the CLI’s MCP integration.</p></div><span class="example-link">Connect a tool <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="release-section shell" aria-labelledby="release-title">
      <div class="release-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Next release</p><h2 id="release-title">More ways to use the same foundation.</h2><p>We’re preparing guides for existing HTTP services, durable coordination, and a second agent example alongside the expanded language APIs.</p></div>
      <div class="release-topics">
        <article><h3>Aster Expose</h3><p>Connect an existing HTTP service to an Aster peer, or publish it through a public HTTPS edge. The edge has its own infrastructure and TLS requirements.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Coordination</h3><p>Maintain one authoritative owner or active version across a small group of persistent nodes. Use leases and fencing where conflicting work would be unsafe.</p></article>
        <article><h3>AgentXchange <span class="planned">Proposed example</span></h3><p>A daemon on each machine receives durable messages and triggers locally configured AI agents. The example is planned; it is not available to run yet.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="languages-section shell" aria-labelledby="languages-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Language surfaces</p><h2 id="languages-title">Choose the API that fits your application.</h2><p>Rust is the first-class facade over Aster’s shared engine. Python, TypeScript, and the FFI bindings expose that foundation in their own runtime’s idioms.</p></div>
      <div class="language-list" aria-label="Languages covered by the release documentation">{languages.map((language) => (
        <span class="language-item"><span class="language-logo"><img src={`/languages/${language.logo}`} alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>{language.name}</span>
      ))}</div>
      <p class="language-note">The next release will document each language’s installation, supported features, and platforms. The current <a href={`${docs}/docs/`}>documentation</a> covers the published entry points.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="closing shell"><div><h2>Try a call between two machines.</h2><p>Start with the quickstart, then add the pieces your application needs.</p></div><a class="start-link" href={`${docs}/docs/quickstart/python`}>Open the quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer shell"><div><a class="footer-name" href="/">Aster</a><span>Enterprise peer-to-peer application SDK.</span></div><div><a href="/blog/why-i-built-aster">Why I built Aster</a><span>© {year} Emrul Islam</span></div></footer>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(body) { background: #0e151e; }
  :global(html) { scroll-padding-top: 24px; }
  :global(.shell) { max-width: 1160px; width: calc(100% - 80px); }
  .site-header { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 30px; padding-top: 27px; padding-bottom: 27px; border-bottom: 1px solid #a5b3c21f; }
  .wordmark { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-size: 23px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  .wordmark :global(.brand-mark) { width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 7px; box-shadow: none; }
  nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 26px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--mist); }
  nav a:hover, .text-link:hover { color: var(--cloud-strong); }
  .intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: 54px; align-items: center; padding-top: 88px; padding-bottom: 68px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 22px; color: var(--relay); font: 11px/1.5 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(44px, 5.1vw, 66px); line-height: 1.06; font-weight: 560; letter-spacing: -.052em; margin: 0 0 28px; color: var(--cloud-strong); }
  .lede { max-width: 45ch; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--cloud); margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .intro-detail { max-width: 48ch; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--mist); margin: 0; }
  .intro-diagram { margin-top: 20px; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 22px; margin-top: 30px; }
  .start-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 24px; padding: 13px 17px; border: 1px solid #7ba2be; border-radius: 5px; background: #bfd5e8; color: #101b27; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; transition: background .15s; }
  .start-link:hover { background: #deebf7; }
  .text-link { color: var(--cloud); font-size: 13px; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 5px; text-decoration-color: #66788e; }
  .foundation { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 32px; padding-top: 20px; padding-bottom: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #a5b3c21f; border-bottom: 1px solid #a5b3c21f; }
  .foundation p { margin: 0; font: 11px var(--mono); color: var(--mist); }
  .foundation a { font-size: 13px; }
  .foundation a span { color: var(--mist); margin-left: 5px; font-size: 12px; }
  .foundation button { margin-left: auto; padding: 5px 0; border: 0; background: none; color: var(--mist); font: 11px var(--mono); cursor: pointer; }
  .call-section, .examples-section { padding-top: 74px; padding-bottom: 74px; }
  h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(27px, 2.8vw, 36px); font-weight: 520; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -.035em; color: var(--cloud-strong); }
  .section-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.25fr 1fr; align-items: end; gap: 72px; margin-bottom: 30px; }
  .section-heading .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .section-heading > p, .section-copy { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--mist); margin: 0; }
  .identity-section { border-top: 1px solid #a5b3c21f; border-bottom: 1px solid #a5b3c21f; background: #111b26; padding: 68px 0; }
  .identity-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr; gap: 110px; }
  .identity-layout .section-copy { margin: 24px 0; max-width: 40ch; }
  .identity-details { margin: 0; }
  .identity-details div { padding: 0 0 23px; margin-bottom: 23px; border-bottom: 1px solid #a5b3c21f; }
  .identity-details div:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; margin-bottom: 0; border: 0; }
  dt { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 15px; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 550; color: var(--cloud-strong); }
  dt span { font: 11px var(--mono); color: var(--relay); }
  dd { margin: 10px 0 0 30px; color: var(--mist); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .example-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 35px 1fr auto; align-items: start; gap: 18px; padding: 28px 0; border-top: 1px solid #a5b3c22f; }
  .example-row:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid #a5b3c22f; }
  .example-number { font: 12px var(--mono); color: var(--mist); padding-top: 6px; }
  h3 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 540; letter-spacing: -.025em; color: var(--cloud-strong); margin: 0 0 9px; }
  .example-row p { max-width: 58ch; margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--mist); }
  .example-link { font-size: 12px; color: var(--relay); padding-top: 7px; }
  .example-row:hover h3 { color: var(--relay); }
  .release-section { border-top: 1px solid #a5b3c21f; padding-top: 52px; padding-bottom: 62px; }
  .release-heading { max-width: 72ch; }
  .release-heading .eyebrow { color: #c0b390; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .release-heading > p:last-child { color: var(--mist); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 18px 0 32px; }
  .release-topics { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 40px; }
  .release-topics article { border-top: 1px solid #a5b3c22f; padding-top: 20px; }
  .release-topics h3 { font-size: 18px; }
  .release-topics p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--mist); margin: 0; }
  .planned { display: block; font: 10px var(--mono); color: #c0b390; margin-top: 7px; letter-spacing: .01em; }
  .languages-section { padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 56px; border-top: 1px solid #a5b3c21f; }
  .languages-section > div:first-child { max-width: 68ch; }
  .languages-section .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .languages-section p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--mist); }
  .language-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 15px 28px; margin: 30px 0 22px; font: 17px var(--mono); color: var(--cloud); }
  .language-item { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
  .language-logo { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 28px; height: 28px; flex: 0 0 28px; overflow: hidden; }
  .language-logo img { width: 28px; height: 28px; object-fit: contain; }
  /* The official Java asset includes a wordmark; show its cup in the common icon slot. */
  .language-logo:has(img[src$="java.png"]) { justify-content: flex-start; }
  .language-logo img[src$="java.png"] { width: 53px; max-width: none; flex-shrink: 0; clip-path: inset(0 32px 0 0); transform: translateX(4px); }
  .languages-section .language-note { font-size: 13px; max-width: 85ch; }
  .language-note a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; color: var(--cloud); }
  .closing { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 32px; padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 48px; border-top: 1px solid #a5b3c22f; }
  .closing h2 { font-size: 28px; }
  .closing p { margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--mist); }
  .closing .start-link { flex-shrink: 0; }
  .site-footer { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 32px; border-top: 1px solid #a5b3c21f; padding-top: 26px; padding-bottom: 94px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--mist); }
  .site-footer div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  .site-footer div:last-child { text-align: right; }
  .footer-name { color: var(--cloud); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 550; }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) { .intro { gap: 24px; } .foundation { gap: 20px; } .foundation a span { display: none; } .identity-layout { gap: 50px; } .section-heading { gap: 36px; } .example-link { max-width: 130px; line-height: 1.6; } }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { :global(.shell) { width: calc(100% - 40px); } .site-header { gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 20px 0; } nav { gap: 16px; font-size: 12px; } .intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding-top: 52px; padding-bottom: 34px; gap: 24px; } h1 { font-size: 49px; } .lede { font-size: 18px; } .intro-diagram { margin: 0; max-width: 540px; width: 100%; } .foundation { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 18px; } .foundation p { width: 100%; } .foundation button { margin-left: 0; } .section-heading, .identity-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; } .call-section, .examples-section { padding: 50px 0; } .identity-section { padding: 48px 0; } .identity-layout h2 br { display: none; } .identity-layout .section-copy { max-width: none; } .identity-details { margin-top: 15px; } .example-row { grid-template-columns: 24px 1fr; gap: 12px; } .example-link { grid-column: 2; max-width: none; padding-top: 0; } .release-topics { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; } .release-section { padding: 44px 0; } .closing { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; } .site-footer { flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; } .site-footer div:last-child { text-align: left; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { :global(html) { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
</style>
<script>
  const motionToggle = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-motion-toggle]');
  if (motionToggle) {
    motionToggle.hidden = false;
    const reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    if (reduced) {
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-motion-paused', '');
      motionToggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');
      motionToggle.textContent = 'Reduced motion';
      motionToggle.disabled = true;
    }
    motionToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const paused = document.documentElement.toggleAttribute('data-motion-paused');
      motionToggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(paused));
      motionToggle.textContent = paused ? 'Resume motion' : 'Pause motion';
    });
  }
</script>
